{"id":"BMGT289D","title":"Frauds, Scams, and Thefts: What, How and Why?","department":"Business and Management","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"\"Why\" does fraud happen? \"How\" does society address fraud? And \"What\" can you do to avoid and prevent fraud in your personal and future career life? This course is designed to give future professionals and managers of all disciplines a general background of fraud. Topics include the psychology of fraud, the mechanics of fraud, the legal landscape, securities fraud, cybercrime, and what all of us should know to protect ourselves from becoming victims of fraud. Additionally, students experience 21st century lessons in fraud examination that have practical application to our daily lives: avoiding cognitive biases, interviewing techniques, basic business controls, and opening our minds to see what others might miss...the red flags of fraud.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":1,"seats":60,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["David Weber"],"removed":false},{"term":"201808","sections":2,"seats":120,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["David Weber"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":2,"seats":130,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":1,"seats":63,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":2,"seats":130,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":1,"seats":65,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":2,"seats":120,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":2,"seats":130,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Samuel Handwerger"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections"